1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. Bg5 e6 7. Qd2 a6 8. O-O-O h6 9. Nxc6 bxc6 10. Bf4 d5 11. Qe3 Bb4 12. Be2 $5 O-O (12... Qa5 13. Be5 Bxc3 14. Bxc3 Qxa2 15. Bd3 dxe4 16. Bxf6 gxf6 (16... exd3 17. Bxg7 Rg8 18. Qxh6 $14) 17. Bxe4 Qa1+ 18. Kd2 Qa5+ 19. c3 $14) 13. e5 Nd7 14. a3 $5 (14. Qg3 Bxc3 (14... Kh8 15. Rd3 (15. Qh3 Bxc3 (15... Kg8 16. Rd3 Ra7 17. Rg3 f6 18. Be3 (18. Qxe6+ Kh8 19. Qxc6 d4 20. Bd3 $16) 18... c5 19. Qxe6+ Kh8 20. Nxd5 Nxe5 21. Qb6 $18) 16. Qxc3 Qb6) (15. Rd4 Be7 16. Be3 c5 17. Rg4 Rg8 18. Bf4 c4 {looks interesting}) 15... Qe7 (15... Nc5 16. Rd4 Bxc3 17. Qxc3 Ne4 18. Qe3 Qa5 19. Rd3 Bd7 (19... g5 20. Ra3 $18) 20. Ra3 Qb4 21. f3 Ng5 22. c3 $16) 16. a3 Ba5 17. Qh3 f6 18. exf6 Nxf6 19. Be5 Bc7 20. Qg3 Bxe5 21. Qxe5 Nd7 22. Qg3 e5 23. Rhd1 e4 24. Re3 Nc5 25. Bh5 Rf5 26. Bg4 Rg5 27. h3 Kg8 28. f3 h5 29. fxe4 hxg4 30. exd5 gxh3 31. Qf4 Qf6 32. Qxf6 gxf6 33. gxh3 Bb7 {0-1 Dumouchel,A-Dushin,A/ICCF Email 2001/ICCF Telchess CBM 96}) 15. Qxc3 Rb8 16. Qg3 Kh8 {and it is hard to find any advantage!}) 14... Be7 (14... Ba5 15. h4 (15. Qg3 Kh8 $13) 15... f6 16. exf6 Qxf6 17. Bd6) 15. h4 $5 {Trying to be creative.} (15. Qg3 $13) 15... Bc5 (15... Rb8 $2 16. Bxh6 gxh6 17. Rh3 Bxh4 18. Rdh1 Bg5 19. f4 Qb6 20. Qg3 Qxb2+ 21. Kd2 Nc5 (21... d4 22. Na4 $18) 22. fxg5 Qxc3+ 23. Qxc3 Ne4+ 24. Kd3 Nxc3 25. Kxc3 c5 26. Rxh6 Kg7 27. Bd3 Rg8 28. Rf6 $18) (15... Qc7 $5) 16. Qg3 Kh8 {Critical position. How to launch an attack?} 17. Bg5 (17. Na4 $5) (17. Rh3) 17... f6 18. Be3 $2 {Clerical error. Forgot to take first!} (18. exf6 Nxf6 19. Bf4 Nd7 {Hard to find any advantage!}) 18... Bxe3+ 19. fxe3 Nxe5 {Lost a pawn, but still there is hope for a king attack!} 20. Qf4 Qd6 {From here on black may have other alternatives, but white could also get a strong attack on the kingside.} (20... Qc7 21. g4 Rf7) (20... c5 21. g4 Nf7) 21. g4 c5 22. Rhg1 Bd7 (22... Rb8 23. g5 $1 fxg5 24. Qg3 g4 25. Ne4 Qc7 26. Nxc5 h5 27. Rdf1 Rxf1+ 28. Rxf1 g5 29. Qf2 $14) 23. g5 fxg5 24. Qg3 Nf7 25. Qxd6 Nxd6 26. hxg5 Rf2 {now I started feeling more comfortable again.} (26... Nf5 $5) 27. gxh6 gxh6 28. Rg6 Nf7 29. Rdg1 Rh2 30. Bxa6 Ng5 31. Rf1 Be8 32. Rf8+ Kh7 33. Rgg8 Rxa6 34. Rh8+ (34. Rxe8 {was an interesting alternative, but I felt I could gain a crucial tempo by putting the opponents king in front of his free pawn!}) 34... Kg6 35. Rhg8+ Kh5 36. Rxe8 d4 37. exd4 cxd4 38. Nd1 Rc6 39. c3 Ne4 40. Rc8 $1 Rxc8 41. Rxc8 d3 42. a4 {the most straightforward move. Other attempts may easily lose.} Rc2+ 43. Kb1 Rd2 $1 {black has to be careful!} (43... Re2 $2 44. Rd8 Re1 45. Rxd3 Nf2 46. Rd6 Nxd1 47. Ka2 {and white is winning!}) 44. Kc1 (44. Ne3 Re2 45. Nc4 {does not lead anywhere for white}) 44... Kg4 45. a5 {the simplest draw!} Kf3 46. Rg8 Ke2 47. Rg2+ Ke1 48. Rg1+ 1/2-1/2

